mhn|n|The quantity of medicine given, or prescribed to be taken, at one time. ; A sufficient quantity; a portion; as much as one can take, or as falls to one to receive. ; Anything nauseous that one is obliged to take; a disagreeable portion thrust upon one. ; To proportion properly (a medicine), with reference to the patient or the disease; to form into suitable doses. ; To give doses to; to medicine or physic to; to give potions to, constantly and without need. ; To give anything nauseous to.	a:16v1,130,1~16v1,130,1
