ml0|n|Fine, soft, hairy outgrowth from the skin or surface of animals or plants, not matted and fleecy like wool ; The soft under feathers of birds. They have short stems with soft rachis and bards and long threadlike barbules, without hooklets. ; The pubescence of plants; the hairy crown or envelope of the seeds of certain plants, as of the thistle. ; The soft hair of the face when beginning to appear. ; That which is made of down, as a bed or pillow; that which affords ease and repose, like a bed of down	V:29v3,1,2~29v3,1,2
